post-it: Stops before Windows starts
cause: Bad RAM module
symptoms:
	Stops before Windows starts
	Error text at startup
	Restarts by itself
	Blue screen
checks:
	no: Windows starts
	no: Memory test passes
		shows: fails with "Memory test fail", then "System halted"
	yes: Shows a picture at power-on
	no: Stops at "Non-System disk or disk error"
	no: Floppy in drive A:
	yes: CPU fan is clean and spins freely
	no: CPU fan is clogged or blocked
	no: GPU heatsink is scorched
	yes: Every part sits in its own place
	no: CPU socket is empty
	no: Fans run but no picture
hardware steps:
	Open case
	Swap one RAM module for a new one
	Power on and watch the memory test
	If it still fails, put that module back and swap the other
	Trash the bad module
	Close case
notes:
	Nothing on the modules shows which one is bad: the player finds it by swapping one and switching the computer on.
